{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563433-boston-the-white","id":1563433,"title":"Boston the White","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-24T14:37:13-07:00","id":1563433,"title":"Boston the White","content":"I wanted to present my column to you:<br /> \ud83e\ude78 <b>BOSTON THE WHITE \u2014 Vampire: The Masquerade Chronicle (V20)</b><br /> <i>&quot;The Abyss did not keep us.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Boston: 2019.</b><br /> In 1988, five people disappeared into the Umbra during a confrontation engineered by a master manipulator. They returned twenty years later. Except they had lived for more than 350 years in a realm where time does not flow as it should.<br /> What they endured there transformed them, bound them together, and made them capable of things no Kindred in Boston had ever dared to imagine.<br /> A few months after their discreet return, the city's established powers \u2014 Ventrue, Malkavians, Giovanni, Nosferatu \u2014 fell within a matter of hours. Silently. With virtually no resistance.<br /> The members of the <b>Sombre Voyage</b> had seized power.<br /> Since then, an unknown Prince, virtually unheard of by the rest of the Camarilla, has ruled Boston with an almost unsettling efficiency.<br /> His name is <b>Gabriel S\u00e9rack</b>.<br /> Officially, he is Brujah.<br /> Unofficially, even the Camarilla dares not make a definitive judgment.<br /> <b>A city that learned to reinvent itself</b><br /><br /> Ten years.<br /> That is how long it took the Circle to transform a silent conquest into an invisible architecture. Nothing in Boston is left to chance.<br /> The city's vampires no longer hide in ruins and forgotten cemeteries. They have learned to become modernity itself in order to control it.<br /> Some Kindred sit on corporate boards, finance foundations, and oversee municipal programs. The city has become greener, more open, more modern.<br /> Every &quot;progressive&quot; policy conceals a second meaning that only insiders can perceive: fewer streetlights to make hunting in the shadows easier; declining religious belief to weaken True Faith; carefully cultivated migration flows and anonymous crowds serving as a permanent feeding ground.<br /> Even environmentalism serves the Blood.<br /> A vampire who ignores a smartphone or a modern surveillance camera is a dead vampire.<br /> <b>Boston the White has made adaptation a doctrine of state \u2014 and the city itself an organism entirely designed to feed, protect, and conceal those who rule it.</b><br /> <i>&quot;Kindred who ignore this century will not survive it. They will simply disappear, politely, without anyone noticing their absence.&quot;</i><br /> <b>A city held together by an impossible truce</b><br /><br /> The Prince does not rule the night alone.<br /> Somewhere beneath Fenway, in the underground levels of an old building, a handful of werewolves and the vampire Prince once sealed an agreement that neither side should ever have accepted:<br /> <b>The Fenway Pact.</b><br /> A survival truce against the Black Spiral Dancers and the corruption of the Wyrm.<br /> Not friendship. Never trust.<br /> But an equilibrium that holds for as long as Boston does.<br /> <i>&quot;I don't like you, Prince. But I'd rather deal with a serpent that keeps its word than a hyena that smiles.&quot;</i><br /> This fragile agreement rests upon bonds far older than the city's conquest: bonds forged in the Umbra itself, between a vampire and a Garou who had broken with her own tribe, between a Silver Fang warrior and Kinfolk who became Kindred against their will.<br /> What the Sombre Voyage truly created, no one in Boston fully suspects.<br /> <b>What awaits you</b><br /><br /><ul><li><b>A Circle of vampires</b> united by a past that no mortal \u2014 and most Kindred \u2014 could ever believe.</li> <li><b>A vampire-werewolf truce</b> as precious as it is fragile, where each side counts its common enemies more carefully than its allies.</li> <li><b>A city-laboratory</b>, where urban planning, culture, and public policy are all tools serving a nocturnal order.</li> <li><b>A dense political court:</b> Clan Council, ghoul networks, and shadow diplomacy between rival domains.</li> <li><b>Secrets within secrets</b>, where even insiders never know the whole truth \u2014 and where those who dig too deeply may discover that Boston was perhaps never anything more than a mechanism in someone else's hands.</li> </ul><b>And now?</b><br /><br /> Since the <b>Beckoning</b>, the silent call that emptied the city of its elder vampires, the Sabbat has continued to collapse in on itself, city after city.<br /> Boston, however, has never wavered.<br /> Elsewhere in New England, some are only beginning to wonder how.<br /> And why such a young city has remained standing where so many others have fallen.<br /> <b>Did we wait too long to become concerned about Boston the White?</b><br /> <i>&quot;The world changes faster than our habits. I chose to change faster than the world. Boston is not my city: it is my proof.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Gabriel S\u00e9rack</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T13:34:03-07:00","id":1563477,"title":"","content":"I think in English you usually put the color before the noun. You'd say 'White Boston', instead of 'Boston the White' which sounds a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Anyway is this an old chronicle you played?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T16:03:29-07:00","id":1563480,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I'm French. I make mistakes in English. Yes, it's a column I've been performing for a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T18:52:18-07:00","id":1563483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563433-boston-the-white?p=1563477#post1563477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in English you usually put the color before the noun. You'd say 'White Boston', instead of 'Boston the White' which sounds a bit odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends if it is an adjective or an epithet.<br /> <br /> In the first case you're correct, but in the second Boston the White is the correct one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T23:17:29-07:00","id":1563488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkantar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563433-boston-the-white?p=1563480#post1563480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm French. I make mistakes in English. Yes, it's a column I've been performing for a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I accept your apology for being French.<br /> <br /> Anyway it sounds cool, were in the umbra did the vamps end up? Or was that a background thing?<br /> <br /> How did they convince the werewolves to sign a pact with them?<br /> <br /> Also in English I think column is chronicle, not sure there's a definite language barrier here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T08:44:58-07:00","id":1563498,"title":"","content":"Story Context : The story begins with the characters' arrival in Boston, ten years after Prince Gabriel Serack seized control of the city, in a context marked by Beckoning and numerous clan movements within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The characters are Elders who discover a city where vampires are &quot;educated&quot; in modernity and new technologies.<br /> Boston is ruled by the prince and his three children.<br /> <br /> His sons, Michael Cannon and Caleb Reece, are Elders. His daughter, Dolores Nickols, has just been created. A fourth child of the prince, young Samuel Lorca, seems to have disappeared without explanation.<br /> <br /> In reality, Gabriel made him disappear after discovering that Samuel had physically and psychologically manipulated a child in order to frame the priest in charge of the New Inquisition for pedophilia. This plot is inspired by a real case that affected Boston.<br /> <br /> One of the characters is in Boston at the request of a high-ranking Camarilla official. Another has come to find out what happened to the Giovanni clan members in the city. The others believe they have greater freedom and have come to Boston for their own reasons.<br /> Over time, the characters will discover that the members of the Circle (the prince and his two sons) have left, accompanied by two other individuals, two werewolves, to undertake a Dark Journey into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> This Dark Journey was organized by Japhet to free the Harbingers of Skulls and conduct an experiment to manipulate a group.<br /> <br /> Why the &quot;Fenway Pact&quot;?<br /> <br /> 1. The Location of the First Meeting<br /> The initial secret negotiations reportedly took place in the Fenway district, near the famous Red Sox stadium.<br /> At that time, a pack of Black Spiral Dancers was preparing a major attack on Boston. Gabriel S\u00e9rack and the local Garou then supposedly concluded a temporary truce in the basement of an old building in the neighborhood.<br /> The few in the know have since referred to this agreement as:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Fenway Pact&quot;<br /> 2. A Boston Symbol<br /> Fenway Park is one of the city's most recognizable symbols.<br /> Over time, the pact's name has become shorthand for a simple idea:<br /> <br /> &quot;What protects Boston above all else.&quot;<br /> Even those unfamiliar with the treaty's details understand what this expression means.<br /> <br /> 3. An Irony S\u00e9rack Appreciates<br /> Gabriel probably appreciates this name precisely because it seems so commonplace.<br /> If a vampire mentions the &quot;Fenway Pact&quot; to a mortal, the mortal will immediately think of baseball.<br /> It is therefore an excellent code name for preserving the Masquerade.<br /> The pact is known only within the few circles that are aware of its existence.<br /> <br /> This is neither an alliance nor a friendship.<br /> <br /> It's a survival pact.<br /> The Garou protect Boston from the Wyrm's forces. Gabriel S\u00e9rack protects Boston from predators who might take advantage of the chaos.<br /> Neither side truly trusts the other.<br /> <br /> But both know that a victory for the Black Spiral Dancers would likely mean the city's downfall.<br /> <br /> A city designed to be protected<br /> Gabriel S\u00e9rack quickly understands that a sustainable city is also a city that is easier to protect. Reducing light pollution, limiting certain intrusive technologies, preserving natural spaces, and revitalizing certain neighborhoods thus become policies supported by both the Circle and the Garou, but for different reasons.<br /> For the vampires, these measures allow for greater control of their domain, more effective surveillance, and a reduction of the risks to the Masquerade.<br /> For the Garou, they are a way to limit the Weaver and Wyrm's hold on Boston.<br /> <br /> Thus, without ever becoming true allies, the two sides gradually contribute to shaping a single city.<br /> <br /> A cleaner, more controlled, more modern city.<br /> <br /> And above all, a city that can survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","user":"Elkantar","date":". 08-27-2026, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T10:16:55-07:00","id":1563540,"title":"","content":"The goal is to talk about Vampire: The Masquerade, not so much to receive an English lesson. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T12:49:54-07:00","id":1563543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkantar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563433-boston-the-white?p=1563540#post1563540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal is to talk about Vampire: The Masquerade, not so much to receive an English lesson. \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you mentioned the plot was to free the Harbingers of skulls so did any PC play one or did they feature as npcs? How did they work in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-27T13:53:59-07:00","id":1563545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563433-boston-the-white?p=1563543#post1563543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you mentioned the plot was to free the Harbingers of skulls so did any PC play one or did they feature as npcs? How did they work in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wish, I could tell you about the dark journey that is the preamble to the chronicle. <br /> The Dark Journey runs from 1988 to 2009.<br /> It led to the liberation of the Harbingers of Skulls.<br /> The journey is actually brought about by Japheth, a 4th generation vampire and distinguished magician.<br /> By a spell, Japhet casts two groups of opposing NPCs into the Umbra.<br /> They are thrown into the Realm Flow, a realm of the Umbra where time is not fixed and flows erratically.<br /> The journey ends in 2009.<br /> The PJ chronicle begins 10 years later, around 2019, after the return of the five NPCs and their takeover of Boston.<br /> <br /> No PCs were Harbinger of Skulls.<br /> On the other hand, the PCs were able to study the consequences of the Harbingers' return, including the disappearance of the Vampire community Giovanni from Boston.<br /> It would have been perfectly possible, in the design of the chronicle, to integrate a PJ Harbinger of Skulls.<br /> The Harbingers of Skulls are not the main protagonists of the Dark Journey, but their release is one of its major consequences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T19:29:28-07:00","id":1563738,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><b>AI is not permitted on these forums in any way shape or form. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}